📌 AI-Powered Intrusion Detection & Prevention System (IDS-IPS)

An AI-based cybersecurity system that detects and prevents malicious network
activity using Machine Learning.
The system supports both offline analysis (CSV) and real-time live network
monitoring, with an interactive visualization dashboard.

🚀 Project Overview

This project implements a complete Intrusion Detection System (IDS) combined
with an Intrusion Prevention System (IPS) using Machine Learning.

The system:

=> Detects network attacks using a trained Random Forest model
=> Prevents suspicious activity using a lightweight IPS logic
=> Supports two modes:
    => File Mode (CSV / Dataset)
    => Live Mode (Real packet capture)
=> Displays real-time monitoring through a Streamlit dashboard
=> Maintains security logs
=> Provides visual analytics (graphs, counters, charts)

🧠 Machine Learning Model

=> Dataset used: NSL-KDD
=> Features: 41 network features
=> Model: Random Forest Classifier
=> Preprocessing: StandardScaler
=> Attack Classes:
    => DoS (Denial of Service)
    => Probe (Scanning / Reconnaissance)
    => R2L (Remote to Local)
    => U2R (User to Root)


Saved model files:
* ids_model.pkl
* scaler.pkl

🛡️ System Architecture
           ┌──────────────┐
           │   Frontend   │
           │ Streamlit UI │
           └──────┬───────┘
                  │
                  ▼
           ┌──────────────┐
           │   Backend    │
           │ ML + IPS     │
           └──────┬───────┘
                  │
      ┌───────────┼───────────┐
      ▼                       ▼
 File Mode                Live Mode
 (CSV Streaming)       (Packet Capture)
      ▼                       ▼
 Detection (ML) → Prevention (IPS) → Logging → Visualization

⚙️ Features

IDS (Detection):

=> Detects multiple attack types using ML
=> Works on offline and live traffic
=> Real-time prediction

IPS (Prevention):

=> Blocks repeated malicious patterns
=> Maintains prevention memory
=> Logs actions to security_log.csv

Modes:

* File Mode → Upload CSV → Detect + Prevent
* Live Mode → Capture real network packets → Detect + Prevent

Dashboard:

=> Real-time monitoring
=> Start / Stop control
=> Attack distribution chart
=> Live activity timeline
=> Blocked vs Allowed counters
=> Security logs

