🖥️ Installation
1. Clone repository
git clone https://github.com/yourusername/ai-ids-ips.git
cd ai-ids-ips
2. Install dependencies
pip install streamlit scikit-learn pandas numpy plotly joblib scapy
3. Install Npcap (Windows only for live mode)
Download from: https://npcap.com/#download
Enable WinPcap compatibility mode during install.

▶️ Run the Project
python -m streamlit run ids_dashboard.py

Open browser → Dashboard starts.

📊 How to Use

File Mode:
1. Upload CSV file
2. System detects attacks
3. IPS blocks suspicious traffic
4. Visualizations update

Live Mode:
1. Click Start Live Monitoring
2. Open browser / generate network traffic
3. System captures packets in real time
4. Detection + Prevention occurs live
5. Click Stop to pause

📜 Security Logs

All detected/prevented events are saved in:

"logs/security_log.csv"

Contains:

-Timestamp
-Attack type
-Action (ALLOWED / BLOCKED)

⚠️ Limitations

=> Live mode uses lightweight feature extraction (not full flow features)
=> Accuracy in live capture may be lower than dataset mode
=> Not intended for production-grade deployment
=> Designed for academic and research purposes

🔮 Future Improvements

=> Flow-based feature extraction (CICFlowMeter style)
=> Real firewall blocking
